  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NESA Community Oriented Policing and Countering Violent Extremism Seminar 01-22A</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The NESA Community Oriented Policing and Countering Violent Extremism Seminar is intended to build stronger relationships with security practitioners in South Asia and Middle East. The primary objective of the seminar is to promote dialogue and regional cooperation among rising security leaders in the region. The seminar is intended to broaden participants understanding of local and regional civilian law enforcement strategies to deal with the threat of extremism through engagement with distinguished scholars, U.S. policy advisors, and U.S. defense personnel. Some of the results will be unique insights gained from these practitioners in the region, as well as the creation of a professional network of government, military, and academic leaders better prepared to engage in the international community. This course will focus on these challenges of institutionalizing COP for CVE, so that the COP approach can be employed as a key tool to counter violent extremism keeping in view local needs and cultural contexts.</narrative>
  </description>
